Debian packaging baseline
=========================

This directory is based on the Debian 12 packaging for
dante 1.4.2+dfsg-7.  Ubuntu 22.04's 1.4.2+dfsg-7build4 packaging was
also checked; the only difference between the two official debian.tar.xz
archives is debian/changelog.  Download locations and the SHA-256 values
published by their .dsc files are recorded in upstream-packaging.sha256.

The packaging is applied to newer upstream Dante sources.  The
configure.patch context was refreshed for the current configure.ac.  The
already-applied method_uname.c hunk was removed from cppcheck.patch.
sa_siginfo.patch (non-Linux portability) was omitted because parts of it are
already upstream and its remaining hunks do not apply to the current sources.
typos.patch retains only the danted.conf template hunk so the package installs
the same configuration bytes as Debian 12; its other fixes are already
upstream or no longer apply.  The target package platforms are Linux on amd64
and arm64.

The two pam.servicename documentation hunks were removed from
rename-programs.patch.  Renaming the executable and service does not change
Dante's compiled DEFAULT_PAMSERVICENAME, which remains sockd; keeping that
default also preserves existing host PAM policies during an upgrade.

Current configure output creates config-parser links in dlib/ and sockd/.
debian/rules removes those links before copying the generated parser sources,
preserving the intent of the Debian 1.4.2 packaging on current sources.

The dante-server package continues to depend on lsb-base because Ubuntu 22.04
ships /lib/lsb/init-functions there.  Debian 12 treats lsb-base as a
transitional package to sysvinit-utils, so the corresponding Lintian error is
overridden for this cross-distribution package.

The package uses the 3.0 (quilt) source format.  dpkg-buildpackage applies the
patch series automatically.
